 { { col, values = { up to 5 distinct descriptions }, n = executions } } — recorded by the instrumented executor at each action execution (a map by its keys, a scalar typed, the root context named; not inside untaken arms). CART-1310 |\n| How does a request get from this workload to its peer — which line names the peer, which Service port, which selector, which workload listens, is it health-probed — and how do the helm answers change under a stage's values? | `:CartographK8sTrace` in a manifest, cursor in an object: every peer it names, hop by hop at the DECLARING lines (quickfix) — `checkoutservice names cartservice:7070` (env line) → `Service/cartservice port 7070` → `selects Deployment/cartservice` (the selector line) → `Deployment/cartservice listens` (containerPort) → `probed: gRPC health, 2 probes, 3 copies of the contract`; a peer with no Service in the release ends in a `dangling` hop. In Lua `require('cartograph.k8s').traces(data, '<file>::Deployment/x')` → { { peer, hops = { { text, file, line } } } } (over the post-pass graph: object nodes, sited selects / probes edges). A TRACE, never a drawn network. THE STAGE VANTAGE: `:CartographHelmStage -f stages/prd/values.yaml --set …` sets the values set this session sees a chart through; :CartographHelmOrigin / Branch / Dot use it when given no flags (`:CartographHelmStage` shows it, `-` clears it). CART-1316 |\n"}},"verb":"edit","id":"1790924270.438120-edit"},{"invocation":{"touched":["tools/docaudit.lua"],"verb":"edit","args":{"before":"-- The DOC AUDIT — validate cartograph's OWN user documentation against the\n-- code ([[cartograph-shipping-checklist]]: a capability ships → flip the\n-- surfaces, and README/help are two of them). doc/cartograph.txt and README.md\n-- are hand-authored CLAIMS about a surface that grows every session, and\n-- nothing else checks them. The helpdoc drifts fastest because it is the\n-- surface nobody re-reads. PROJECT-MANAGEMENT action: the subject is our own\n-- documentation, n